# SwolleWatch Cursor Rules (.cursorrules)

## Stack & Architecture
- Framework: React Native with Expo (Managed Workflow, SDK 51+)
- Navigation: Expo Router (File-based navigation)
- State Management: Zustand with AsyncStorage persistence
- Styling: NativeWind (Tailwind CSS for React Native)
- Audio/TTS: Native iOS `expo-speech` for Text-To-Speech & `expo-av` for audio chimes
- Language: TypeScript (Strict mode enabled)

## Code Quality & Conventions
1. Keep UI components small, modular, and reusable in `src/components/`.
2. Do NOT use Python, HTML, or FastAPI backend code in this React Native app.
3. Handle dark mode natively using NativeWind class names (`bg-black`, `text-white`, `border-neutral-800`).
4. Ensure all interval timer logic is localized inside a dedicated Zustand store (`useWorkoutStore`).
5. Never hardcode workout segments—allow dynamic array operations (add, edit, remove, reorder).

## AI Behavior
- Keep responses concise and focused purely on React Native / Expo code.
- Always provide complete TypeScript interfaces for state objects.